WEBVTT

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.320
Why? 

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.230
What's this mean? 

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:45.190
Why has Will turned into an enemy? 

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:49.880
Which means that one is... Nick? 

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:55.880
Brother! 

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.960
Brother! 

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.560
Brother! 

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.860
Li...na... 

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:27.370
Will! 

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:28.930
Brother! 

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:30.850
You idiot, don't! 

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:31.270
Lina!

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:32.500
Let go of me!

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.710
My brother... He's... 

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:41.800
Joey! 

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.560
We're gettin' outta here. Now's our chance. 

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.130
No! We can't leave him! 

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:49.570
We're surrounded! 

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:51.560
If we don't escape now we're in trouble! 

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:52.710
No! 

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.530
Brother... 

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.200
Come with me! 

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:11.620
Joey! 

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.580
Ah, well... 

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:55.750
Test subject 01 has malfunctioned. 

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.910
Recall him and 02 immediately. 

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.110
What are we to do with the remainders? 

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.690
They have the territorial advantage. 

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:05.120
We will regroup and rethink our strategy. 

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:08.220
Until then, intensify our surveillance. 

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:09.560
Yes, sir.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:37.630
Lina.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.890
Hey! 

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:52.140
Everyone! 

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:54.730
Professor! 

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:56.480
This is bad! 

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.440
Real bad, everyone! 

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.040
Same for us... 

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.000
<i>All shots were a direct hit... </i>

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:33.780
<i>No damage. </i>

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.340
<i>Not even a scratch... </i>

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:37.060
<i>Is there some reaction? </i>

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.030
<i>No reaction. </i>

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:41.250
<i>The target is simply proceeding 
in a direct line. </i>

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:43.820
<i>Okay. Analysis team, head in front! </i>

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:50.730
<i>Crow 01, we will now begin analysis. </i>

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.660
Unable to identify its composition. 

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:03.500
Unable to identify its internal structure. 

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.330
It's no use. I can't understand a thing. 

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:09.610
Hey, look... 

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:10.390
What's that? 

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.090
Oh, I see. 

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:29.150
But something was weird! 

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:35.090
I think he was only being 
manipulated by them! 

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:37.020
And that's not all, remember? 

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:40.140
He managed to go toe-to-toe with Heroman! 

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.930
They must have done something to his body. 

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:44.890
Oh, no! 

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.930
Okay, I basically get the picture. 

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:54.530
You do? 

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:58.130
Then how can you just be sitting there? 

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:02.470
If getting upset would help 
solve this, I'd do it. 

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:10.920
In order to deal with Will, we'll need 
to come up with some countermeasure. 

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:12.910
What kind of countermeasure? 

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.240
Uh, I don't know yet... 

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:16.380
Look, Joey... 

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:17.320
But! 

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:19.400
Anyway, listen to me. 

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.190
Anyway nothing! Will's in trouble! 

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:23.700
Joey, we've got a ton of 
problems at once here! 

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:25.670
Try and stay a little calm, okay? 

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:28.230
Okay... 

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.170
It's gotten cold... 

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:35.230
But it tastes good.

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.100
Thank you, Professor. 

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:41.400
I'm okay, Joey. 

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:49.760
Will you listen to what I have to say? 

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:50.490
Yes. 

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:55.540
While you were fighting I approached 
the issue at various different angles,

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:59.160
and at the end of my investigation 
I've determined something really bad! 

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.670
Really bad? 

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:03.590
What could that be? 

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:06.810
It's about those spheres... 

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:09.920
Um... 

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.540
You sure I don't need to pedal? 

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:17.350
Yeah. I collected some batteries I can use. 

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:28.940
Currently the five giant spheres that 
were sent forth from the Skrugg's saucer

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:32.470
are each proceeding along at 
a speed of 25 miles per hour. 

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:35.250
Of the five, two of them 
disappeared toward the ocean,

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:38.820
however the other three are moving 
within the American continent. 

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:42.750
The spheres are not affected 
by our attacks at all. 

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.580
We also have been unable to identify the 
construction or internal structure. 

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:54.080
Of the three, one has avoided major population
centers and will soon leave our borders. 

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:56.840
One will shortly enter the ocean. 

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:02.570
However the last one is the problem. 

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:10.360
Listen up. The issue is these spheres 
moving in perfectly straight lines. 

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.060
What's the meaning of it? 

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:15.040
At first glance it seems
like they're just rolling,

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:19.030
but each of the five spheres
has its own destination. 

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:20.670
Really? 

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:21.950
Take a look.

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:28.100
These are the paths of the five spheres 
as they move in straight lines. 

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:34.760
That's... 

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.270
Where? 

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:40.130
Washington D.C. 1600 Pennsylvania Ave... 

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:43.060
The White House! 

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:46.870
That sphere is heading here? 

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:49.450
Yes. There is no mistake. 

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:55.400
If we extend the paths 
of the other spheres... 

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:56.570
Europe,

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.100
Oceania,

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:01.790
Africa,

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:04.370
and Asia... 

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.280
They'll reach each of the five continents. 

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:08.390
If we leave them alone, then 
something really bad is... 

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:09.460
This is bad! 

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:12.000
See? I told you! 

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:16.940
But this is a seriously dire situation. 

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:20.380
They're not just attacking at random. 

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:24.390
They've done plenty of
research on us humans,

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:27.240
and planned out their
method of attack! 

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:40.950
It is currently heading toward an area 
of relatively low population density. 

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:45.920
Mr. President? 

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:48.720
Are you... 

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:54.700
...suggesting we use nuclear weapons? 

00:10:56.620 --> 00:11:00.960
We cannot ignore the saucer 
in Center City either. 

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:04.040
When you think about the future, there 
is only one decision to make... 

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:05.430
Wait! 

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:07.600
How much time do I have until the launch?

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:10.840
It's currently 11 AM. 

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:14.440
You have 9 more hours. 

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:42.690
After looking at the recording,

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:45.930
it seems he received some external
shock to his memory storage area. 

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:52.970
Therefore the primary factor was the damage 
done by the enemy to the controller. 

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:54.940
It would cause such confusion. 

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:04.020
Can you repair him? 

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:05.550
Of course. 

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:09.790
Although it will take 
some time to perfect it. 

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:10.790
Make haste. 

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:18.300
It looks like the white one and the test 
subject have some connection to each other. 

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:28.420
Could things get any worse? 

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:34.040
But even Heroman couldn't fight those 
spheres in five places at once. 

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:40.180
And anyway, we haven't chased off 
the Skrugg here in the city. 

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:43.440
We can't just ignore the White House! 

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:46.080
So you don't care what 
happens to Center City? 

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:48.420
Well, I don't like it obviously... 

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:50.640
Calm down, you two. 

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:53.050
Anyway, let's gather information. 

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:56.310
So that we know what we 
should be doing first! 

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:10.010
Why do they just go straight? 

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:14.280
I wonder why they can only go straight? 

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:17.020
Because they don't need to turn? 

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:17.850
But... 

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:21.300
Wait, what are you trying to say? 

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:25.120
When fighting it I got this weird feeling. 

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:29.250
Like it didn't even notice 
Heroman being there. 

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:32.820
Like it couldn't do anything 
but try to move forward. 

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:37.330
Maybe those spheres don't have any drivers! 

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:38.420
That's it! 

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:45.190
I see! So that's what it is! 

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:46.510
You figured something out?

00:13:47.230 --> 00:13:51.990
All five spheres are going perfectly 
straight at the same speed! 

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:55.960
And the timing of those spikes... 

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:58.020
That's... 

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:00.150
...exactly at the same time! 

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.430
Exactly! 

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:05.360
Those spheres are clearly unmanned weapons! 

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:09.410
Which means they're being 
controlled from the spaceship. 

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:12.950
And therefore, if we can do 
something about that UFO... 

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.660
Exactly! 

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:16.040
...we can stop the spheres! 

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:19.040
And that's where my brother and Nick are! 

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:20.370
Lina! 

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:22.750
That's right, isn't it? 

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:26.600
Yeah, true... 

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:29.150
It's easy to say, but... 

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:33.060
Give me a bit more time. 

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:39.050
Heroman and us three have 
got to do something. 

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:39.810
No! 

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:43.150
Us <i>four</i>! 

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.360
Lina! 

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:52.630
I know it's dangerous, but 
it's my problem, too! 

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:54.530
Please, let me help! 

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:04.870
It'd be our pleasure. 

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:07.050
We need all the help we can get, after all. 

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:09.770
Professor! 

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:10.330
Professor Denton! 

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:13.790
I'll need some time to prepare. 

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:16.850
And you two need your rest. 

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:22.730
Yeah... How many days has it been 
since I got some real sleep? 

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:27.390
I think we'll head out tonight. 

00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:22.020
We gotta do this... 

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:26.460
You're really strong, Lina.  

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:30.240
All the other people have 
long evacuated the city. 

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:32.460
I'm scared too, you know. 

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:37.790
And compared to you, Joey, 
I'm not doing much. 

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:40.290
No, I'm not really... 

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:44.980
Why'd all this happen, I wonder? 

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:49.250
Just a bit before we were 
going to school like normal,

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:54.490
I was going to cheerleader practice like 
normal, playing with my friends like normal... 

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:01.980
Brother... 

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:04.340
Lina... 

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:08.170
I'll definitely... I'll definitely bring Will... 

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:15.050
They found us! 

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:23.560
Joey! 

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:28.690
Run for it! 

00:17:47.740 --> 00:17:48.920
Heroman! 

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:03.870
Lina, hide! 

00:18:04.300 --> 00:18:05.670
Joey! 

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:07.510
I have to fight, too! 

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:23.530
Heroman! 

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:39.900
Heroman! 

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:55.360
Heroman... 

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.480
Blast! 

00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:02.720
We've got to tell the Professor and 
Psy that we've been found, quick! 

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.740
Let's go back, Heroman! 

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:07.390
Heroman! 

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:09.720
Joey! 

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:26.490
Now that they know we're here, 
there's no turning back! 

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:30.240
Ready, everyone?

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:36.500
We're off! 

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:07.410
What is it? 

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:08.530
Mr. President. 

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:11.940
General Watkins would like 
to meet with you urgently. 

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:13.980
Watkins? 

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:16.210
Let him in. 

00:21:20.240 --> 00:21:21.960
Excuse me, Sir. 

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:24.160
What is it, Watkins? 

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:28.270
I hope you've found some method 
other than using nuclear weapons.

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:30.510
About that... 

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:34.270
How do you do, Mr. President? 

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:39.650
I have a suggestion about 
this problem you face. 

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:43.950
So I asked the general to bring me here. 

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:45.070
Who are you? 

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:49.320
Oh, I apologize for the late introduction. 

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.240
My name is Minami. 

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:57.620
Dr. Minami. 
I am most humbled to make your acquaintance. 

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:24.090
<b>"Can you hear this voice?"</b>

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:31.560
<b>I've been calling that, always, from deep within my heart.</b>

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:45.460
<b>Would you, all alone, let another lonely one be next to you?</b>

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:51.010
<b>Because together it's not lonely, it's twoly.</b>

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:56.140
<b>See, you're not alone any longer.</b>

00:22:57.280 --> 00:22:59.990
<b>Just because there's no one next to me</b>

00:22:59.990 --> 00:23:02.540
<b>doesn't mean that I'm lonely!</b>

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:07.740
<b>For someone to notice this pain</b>

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:13.270
<b>that heart must have surely cried.</b>

00:23:13.270 --> 00:23:16.650
<b>Right now, we'll crush to bits</b>

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:20.350
<b>the fortress of our limitless sadness!</b>

00:23:20.350 --> 00:23:24.050
<b>I'll take you with me!</b>

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:27.730
<b>Got it? I'm running through at full power.</b>

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:31.470
<b>To where you're waiting, left behind</b>

00:23:31.470 --> 00:23:34.640
<b>in the place of tears...</b>

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:39.770
<b>I believe in you, with burning passion!</b>

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:43.560
<b>Come to me!</b>

00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:52.920
On the next Heroman: 

00:23:52.920 --> 00:23:56.910
Don't do it, Nick! You're wrong! 
You're completely wrong! 

00:23:56.910 --> 00:24:00.350
To stop the five spheres each heading 
to invade a different continent,

00:24:00.350 --> 00:24:06.670
and in order to rescue Will and Nick, Joey 
and company infiltrate enemy territory. 

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:12.010
But what awaits them there 
is an all too sad reality. 

00:24:12.210 --> 00:24:15.940
Next time Heroman Episode #7: Resistance. 

00:24:15.940 --> 00:24:18.660
Heroman... Attack! 
